  "name": "JSON endpoint with a Webhook and Respond to Webhook",
  "description": "## What it does\n\nExposes `POST /webhook/hello` and answers with JSON built in the workflow. No external service, no credentials — a good first template to prove that webhooks and responses work.\n\n## Try it\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:5678/webhook/hello \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"name\":\"Ada\"}'\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n`responseMode` is set to **Respond to Webhook node**, so the HTTP response is only sent when the workflow reaches the last node. Switch it to *Immediately* if you want the webhook to answer before the rest of the workflow runs. Activate the imported workflow before calling the production `/webhook/hello` URL; the test URL is available while editing.",
